                            "Schools must promote responsible digital citizenship because students need to understand how to manage their digital footprints safely, ethically, and wisely in order to protect their future."
                        </blockquote>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Article Breakdown -->
                    <div class="space-y-4">
                        <h3 class="font-cinzel text-xl text-white flex items-center">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb text-theme-cyan mr-2"></i> Why Managing Your Digital Footprint Matters?
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-theme-light/90 leading-relaxed">
                            As young people spend more hours connected to smartphones, social media, and online platforms, the boundary between our offline lives and digital presence is rapidly disappearing. Many students view the internet merely as a space for entertainment and self-expression, often overlooking the lasting impact of their clicks, likes, and uploads. However, every action taken online forms a permanent digital profile that shapes how the world perceives us.
                        </p>

