                            <h2 class="font-cinzel text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-1">
                                ARGUMENT 2: PROTECTING PERSONAL PRIVACY AND AVOIDING IDENTITY RISKS
                            </h2>
                        </div>

                        <div class="bg-theme-card p-4 rounded-xl border-l-2 border-theme-cyan font-playfair italic text-theme-cyan text-lg">
                            "Protecting personal information from misuse."
                        </div>

                        <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-theme-light/90 leading-relaxed">
                            Oversharing personal details such as home addresses, phone numbers, or daily routines creates serious security risks. Cybercriminals and identity thieves often exploit poorly managed digital footprints to track, harass, or scam teenagers. By practicing careful posting habits and setting strict privacy controls, students safeguard themselves from online predators and identity theft.
                        </p>

                        <!-- Citation & Clickable External Link -->
                        <div class="bg-theme-panel p-5 rounded-xl border border-theme-border text-xs space-y-3">
                            <div class="flex items-center text-theme-cyan font-semibold text-sm">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-user-shield mr-2"></i> Privacy Commissioner of Canada Citation
                            </div>
                            <p class="text-theme-muted italic leading-relaxed">
                                According to the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada, social media, online games, and digital applications collect and use people's personal information. If students do not protect their data, their information may be misused.
                            </p>
